00:06:32,733 --> 00:06:33,733
another list of numbers

440
00:06:34,166 --> 00:06:36,166
which we call the query for this word

441
00:06:36,933 --> 00:06:42,366
this query vector though has a much smaller dimension than the embedding vector say one hundred and twenty eight

442
00:06:42,966 --> 00:06:49,300
computing this query looks like taking a certain Matrix which i'll label wq and multiplying it by the embedding

443
00:06:51,133 --> 00:06:58,400
compressing things a bit let's write that query vector as q and then any time you see me put a Matrix next to an arrow like this one

444
00:06:58,600 --> 00:07:04,866
it's meant to represent that multiplying this Matrix by the Vector at the Arrow's start gives you the Vector at the Arrow's end

445
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:12,766
in this case you multiply this matrix by all of the embeddings in the context producing one query vector for each token

446
00:07:13,733 --> 00:07:16,366
the entries of this matrix are parameters of the model

447
00:07:16,566 --> 00:07:18,933
which means the true behavior is learned from data

448
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:23,666
and in practice what this matrix does in a particular attention head is challenging to parse

449
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:24,800
but for our sake

450
00:07:25,066 --> 00:07:27,366
imagining an example that we might hope that it would learn

451
00:07:27,566 --> 00:07:37,966
we'll suppose that this query Matrix maps the embeddings of nouns to certain directions in this smaller query space that somehow encodes the notion of looking for adjectives in preceding positions

452
00:07:38,933 --> 00:07:41,566
as to what it does to other embeddings who knows

453
00:07:41,733 --> 00:07:44,566
maybe it simultaneously tries to accomplish some other goal with those

454
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:46,800
right now we're laser focused on the nouns

455
00:07:47,333 --> 00:07:54,766
at the same time associated with this is a second Matrix called the key Matrix which you also multiply by every one of the embeddings

456
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:58,666
this produces a second sequence of vectors that we call the keys

457
00:07:59,466 --> 00:08:03,333
conceptually you want to think of the keys as potentially answering the queries

458
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:06,566
this key Matrix is also full of tunable parameters

459
00:08:06,766 --> 00:08:08,100
and just like the query Matrix

460
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:11,466
it maps the embedding vectors to that same smaller dimensional space

461
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:17,100
you think of the keys as matching the queries whenever they closely align with each other

462
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:18,300
in our example

463
00:08:18,333 --> 00:08:26,733
you would imagine that the key Matrix maps the adjectives like fluffy and blue to vectors that are closely aligned with the query produced by the word creature

464
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:30,333
to measure how well each key matches each query

465
00:08:30,533 --> 00:08:34,100
you compute a dot product between each possible key-query pair

466
00:08:34,933 --> 00:08:37,700
i like to visualize a grid full of a bunch of dots

467
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:40,600
where the bigger dots correspond to the larger dot products

468
00:08:40,700 --> 00:08:42,666
the places where the keys and queries align

469
00:08:43,366 --> 00:08:51,200
for our adjective noun example that would look a little more like this where if the keys produced by fluffy and blue really do

470
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:58,333
align closely with the query produced by creature then the dot products in these two spots would be some large positive numbers

471
00:08:59,166 --> 00:09:05,466
in the Lingo machine learning people would say that this means the embeddings of fluffy and blue attend to the embedding of creature

472
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:16,666
by contrast the dot product between the key for some other word like the and the query for creature would be some small or negative value that reflects that these are unrelated to each other

473
00:09:17,766 --> 00:09:23,066
so we have this grid of values that can be any real number from negative infinity to infinity

474
00:09:23,466 --> 00:09:28,566
giving us a score for how relevant each word is to updating the meaning of every other word

475
00:09:29,166 --> 00:09:34,166
